      "explanation": "ƒ(x) = 9x<sup>4</sup> + 12x<sup>3</sup> – 36x<sup>2</sup> + 25\n<br><br>ƒ'(x) = 36x<sup>3</sup> + 36x<sup>2</sup> – 72x\n<br><br>ƒ'(x) = 36x(x<sup>2</sup> + x – 2)\n<br><br>ƒ'(x) = 36x(x + 2)(x - 1)\n<picture><source media=\"(max-width: 320px)\" srcset=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/7km5fk0trpftr/5f0e1eff-71b5-4d0d-a88e-74ee4f331bcb/e9176ef0-dc8c-11e9-acf6-6d09a288f7f2/file-7km5fk0trpfts-320w.jpg\"><img src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/7km5fk0trpftr/5f0e1eff-71b5-4d0d-a88e-74ee4f331bcb/e9176ef0-dc8c-11e9-acf6-6d09a288f7f2/file-7km5fk0trpfts-500w.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Main 2019 (Online) 8th April Morning Slot Mathematics - Application of Derivatives Question 173 English Explanation\"></picture>\n<br><br>While moving\nleft to right on x-axis whenever derivative changes sign from\nnegative to positive, we get local minima, and\nwhenever derivative changes sign from positive\nto negative, we get local maxima.\n<br><br><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.509ex\" height=\"1.251ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -471 667 553\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2234\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2234\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> S<sub>1</sub> = {–2, 1}\n<br><br>S<sub>2</sub> = {0}"
